# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) is a variant of SKQD that replaces the need to choose an ansatz from which to sample bitstrings with an ensemble of time-evolution circuits constructed directly from the target Hamiltonian. This is achieved by subsampling smaller time-evolution operators from the Hamiltonian based on its coefficients, which is known as the qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"
msgstr "Ang [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) ay isang variant ng SKQD na pumapalit sa pangangailangang pumili ng ansatz na pagkukunan ng mga bitstring gamit ang isang ensemble ng mga time-evolution circuit na direktang binuo mula sa target na Hamiltonian. Nakakamit ito sa pamamagitan ng subsampling ng mas maliliit na time-evolution operator mula sa Hamiltonian batay sa mga coefficient nito, na kilala bilang qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial makes use of [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to create the more natural fermionic circuits for the [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503) algorithm, followed by the use of fermionic layout and synthesis passes before plugging the circuits into the traditional Qiskit pipeline for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) para gumawa ng mas natural na mga fermionic circuit para sa [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503) algorithm, na sinusundan ng paggamit ng fermionic layout at synthesis pass bago isalang ang mga circuit sa tradisyonal na Qiskit pipeline para sa pagpapatakbo sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian be of the form:\n"
msgstr "Hayaang ang Hamiltonian ay may anyong:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where, without loss of generality, we require $c_i > 0$ and that the largest eigenvalue of $h_i$ be equal, in absolute value, to $1$. Any signed or complex prefactor is absorbed into $h_i$, so the coefficients $c_i$ are strictly positive weights while the $h_i$ carry the direction of each term. Here $N$ is the number of terms (or, after grouping, the number of groups) in the Hamiltonian; it is a property of the Hamiltonian and is distinct from the number of operators sampled into a single circuit, written $n$ below.\n"
msgstr "kung saan, nang walang pagkawala ng pangkalahatan, hinihingi nating $c_i > 0$ at na ang pinakamalaking eigenvalue ng $h_i$ ay katumbas, sa absolute value, ng $1$. Anumang signed o complex na prefactor ay isinasama sa $h_i$, kaya ang mga coefficient na $c_i$ ay mahigpit na positibong weight habang dala ng mga $h_i$ ang direksyon ng bawat term. Dito, ang $N$ ay ang bilang ng mga term (o, pagkatapos ng grouping, ang bilang ng mga group) sa Hamiltonian; katangian ito ng Hamiltonian at naiiba sa bilang ng mga operator na na-sample sa isang circuit, na isinusulat bilang $n$ sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT algorithm then realizes, for the target time $t$, some operator $V_k$, where $k$ goes from $1 \\cdots K$ and signifies the $k_{th}$ SqDRIFT circuit, defined as:\n"
msgstr "Ang qDRIFT algorithm ay nagre-realize, para sa target na oras na $t$, ng ilang operator na $V_k$, kung saan ang $k$ ay mula $1 \\cdots K$ at tumutukoy sa $k_{th}$ na SqDRIFT circuit, na tinukoy bilang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $n$ is the number of sampled operators per circuit and $K$ is the number of circuits in the ensemble. The product runs over the $n$ draws, not over all $N$ Hamiltonian terms, and because the terms are drawn with replacement, the same $h_i$ can appear more than once in a single $V_k$.\n"
msgstr "Dito, ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga na-sample na operator bawat circuit at ang $K$ ay ang bilang ng mga circuit sa ensemble. Ang product ay tumatakbo sa $n$ na draw, hindi sa lahat ng $N$ term ng Hamiltonian, at dahil ang mga term ay kinukuha nang may replacement, ang parehong $h_i$ ay maaaring lumitaw nang higit sa isang beses sa iisang $V_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity:\n"
msgstr "Ang dami na:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is the $L_1$ norm of the coefficients, so each of the $n$ steps evolves for the same duration $\\lambda t / n$ regardless of which term was drawn. The uniformity of the step angle is the characteristic feature of qDRIFT: a coefficient influences the result through *how often* its term is drawn, not through how far that term is rotated. The indices are sampled from the distribution:\n"
msgstr "ay ang $L_1$ norm ng mga coefficient, kaya ang bawat isa sa $n$ na hakbang ay nag-e-evolve sa parehong tagal na $\\lambda t / n$ anuman ang term na nakuha. Ang pagkakapareho ng step angle ang katangian ng qDRIFT: ang isang coefficient ay nakakaapekto sa resulta sa pamamagitan ng *gaano kadalas* kinukuha ang term nito, hindi sa pamamagitan ng kung gaano kalayo iniikot ang term na iyon. Ang mga index ay sina-sample mula sa distribution na:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the series $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ is a random sequence of term indices drawn from this distribution. Since the $c_i$ are positive and sum to $\\lambda$, this is a normalized probability distribution, and the expectation of the resulting channel over the random draws approximates evolution under $H$, with an error that decreases as $n$ grows. Note that the approximation error depends on $\\lambda$ rather than on the number of terms $N$.\n"
msgstr "kaya ang serye $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ ay isang random na sequence ng mga term index na kinuha mula sa distribution na ito. Dahil ang mga $c_i$ ay positibo at ang kabuuan ay $\\lambda$, ito ay isang normalized na probability distribution, at ang expectation ng resultang channel sa mga random na draw ay humahalintulad sa evolution sa ilalim ng $H$, na may error na bumababa habang lumalaki ang $n$. Tandaan na ang approximation error ay nakasalalay sa $\\lambda$ at hindi sa bilang ng mga term na $N$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The SqDRIFT paper writes the number of terms as $\\mathcal{N}$ and the sequence length as $N$; we use $N$ and $n$ here to keep the two clearly distinct.)\n"
msgstr "(Isinusulat ng SqDRIFT paper ang bilang ng mga term bilang $\\mathcal{N}$ at ang haba ng sequence bilang $N$; ginagamit namin dito ang $N$ at $n$ para manatiling malinaw na magkaiba ang dalawa.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to generate an ensemble of such randomized circuits. After we have created these circuits, similar to how we create a Krylov subspace for different operators, we sample bitstrings from multiple such operators with different time parameters. This ensures a higher overlap between the ground state vectors and sampled bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano gumawa ng ensemble ng mga ganitong randomized na circuit. Pagkatapos nating likhain ang mga circuit na ito, katulad ng paglikha natin ng Krylov subspace para sa iba't ibang operator, nagsa-sample tayo ng mga bitstring mula sa maraming ganoong operator na may iba't ibang time parameter. Tinitiyak nito ang mas mataas na overlap sa pagitan ng mga ground state vector at ng mga na-sample na bitstring.\n"

