# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reading and Preparing the FCIDump**\n"
msgstr "**Pagbasa at Paghahanda ng FCIDump**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this tutorial, we will load up the electronic structure Hamiltonian for nitrogen (N2). There are other ways to create fermionic operators as well.  Refer to the documentation at [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/pydoc/qiskit_fermions.operators.library.html#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library).\n"
msgstr "Para sa tutorial na ito, ilo-load natin ang electronic structure Hamiltonian para sa nitrogen (N2). Mayroon ding ibang paraan para gumawa ng mga fermionic operator.  Sumangguni sa dokumentasyon sa [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/pydoc/qiskit_fermions.operators.library.html#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**About this FCIDump.** The file `N2_sto_3g` describes a nitrogen molecule ($N_2$) in the minimal STO-3G basis at an interatomic separation of 1.09 $\\AA$, the experimental equilibrium bond length. Its header declares `NORB=10`, `NELEC=14`, and `MS2=0`: 10 spatial orbitals (hence 20 spin orbitals, and 20 qubits under Jordan-Wigner), 14 electrons in a spin singlet, so seven $\\alpha$ and seven $\\beta$ electrons. All orbitals are given symmetry label 1, that is, no point-group symmetry is exploited. Being a full-space STO-3G dump, no orbitals are frozen and the correlation space is small enough that an exact FCI reference energy can be computed classically for comparison, as shown in the next cell.\n"
msgstr "**Tungkol sa FCIDump na ito.** Inilalarawan ng file na `N2_sto_3g` ang isang molekula ng nitrogen ($N_2$) sa minimal na STO-3G basis sa interatomic separation na 1.09 $\\AA$, ang eksperimental na equilibrium bond length. Idineklara ng header nito ang `NORB=10`, `NELEC=14`, at `MS2=0`: 10 spatial orbital (kaya 20 spin orbital, at 20 qubit sa ilalim ng Jordan-Wigner), 14 na electron sa spin singlet, kaya pitong $\\alpha$ at pitong $\\beta$ na electron. Ang lahat ng orbital ay binigyan ng symmetry label na 1, ibig sabihin, walang point-group symmetry na ginagamit. Dahil ito ay full-space na STO-3G dump, walang frozen na orbital at sapat na maliit ang correlation space kaya maaaring kompyutin nang classical ang eksaktong FCI reference energy para sa paghahambing, gaya ng ipinapakita sa susunod na cell.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An equivalent file can be regenerated with PySCF:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring muling likhain ang katumbas na file gamit ang PySCF:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the integrals depend on the converged SCF orbitals, a regenerated file might differ from the shipped one in orbital phase or ordering; the total energies are unaffected.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang mga integral ay nakasalalay sa mga converged na SCF orbital, ang muling nalikhang file ay maaaring magkaiba sa ibinigay sa orbital phase o ordering; hindi apektado ang mga kabuuang enerhiya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Obtaining the file.** Find the FCIDump in this [GitHub repository](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/tree/main/docs/tutorials/assets/sqdrift/fcidump_files). You can run the cell below to fetch it into the location the rest of the tutorial expects.\n"
msgstr "**Pagkuha ng file.** Hanapin ang FCIDump sa [GitHub repository](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/tree/main/docs/tutorials/assets/sqdrift/fcidump_files) na ito. Maaari mong patakbuhin ang cell sa ibaba para i-fetch ito sa lokasyong inaasahan ng natitirang bahagi ng tutorial.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First we use the `cisolver` provided by pyscf to get the reference energy. This is the true ground state energy of the molecule we are working with. For this we will first declare `norb` and `nelec`, which are the number of orbitals and the number of electrons, respectively. Then we declare `h1e` and `h2e`, which are the one- and two-electron integrals respectively. All of these will later be used for SQD as well.\n"
msgstr "Una, gagamitin natin ang `cisolver` na ibinigay ng pyscf para makuha ang reference energy. Ito ang tunay na ground state energy ng molekulang pinagtatrabahuhan natin. Para dito, idedeklara muna natin ang `norb` at `nelec`, na ang bilang ng mga orbital at ang bilang ng mga electron, ayon sa pagkakasunod. Pagkatapos ay idedeklara natin ang `h1e` at `h2e`, na ang one- at two-electron integral, ayon sa pagkakasunod. Gagamitin din ang lahat ng ito sa SQD sa susunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Loading the Hamiltonian**\n"
msgstr "**Paglo-load ng Hamiltonian**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the necessary data ready, we read the Hamiltonian from the FCI file in a format that is compatible with `qiskit-fermions`\n"
msgstr "Kapag handa na ang kinakailangang data, babasahin natin ang Hamiltonian mula sa FCI file sa format na compatible sa `qiskit-fermions`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fermionic workflows with `qiskit-fermions`**\n"
msgstr "**Mga fermionic workflow gamit ang `qiskit-fermions`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will first map the Hamiltonian into a fermionic circuit model using `qiskit-fermions`, which provides transpiler passes and gates specific to fermionic circuits. These will later be used before Qiskit's traditional transpiler passes for this workflow.\n"
msgstr "Una nating ime-map ang Hamiltonian sa isang fermionic circuit model gamit ang `qiskit-fermions`, na nagbibigay ng mga transpiler pass at gate na espesipiko sa mga fermionic circuit. Gagamitin ang mga ito sa susunod bago ang mga tradisyonal na transpiler pass ng Qiskit para sa workflow na ito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Term grouping**\n"
msgstr "**Term grouping**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To ensure the reproducibility of results, we first use `canonical_order` to sort the terms based only on their structure. The order of the operators in the `canon` list is therefore fixed. This ensures reproducibility of created operators because the `QDriftTrotterization` pass that we will use in the future samples random indices to create the qDRIFT operators.\n"
msgstr "Para matiyak ang reproducibility ng mga resulta, gagamitin muna natin ang `canonical_order` para i-sort ang mga term batay lang sa istruktura nila. Kaya nakapirmi ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga operator sa listahang `canon`. Tinitiyak nito ang reproducibility ng mga nalikhang operator dahil ang `QDriftTrotterization` pass na gagamitin natin sa hinaharap ay nagsa-sample ng mga random na index para likhain ang mga qDRIFT operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this step, we exploit the many symmetries that are present in the electronic structure Hamiltonian by grouping related terms with identical coefficients. While doing so changes the operator coefficient distribution which the qDRIFT protocol samples from, this does not affect its convergence guarantees. Crucially, grouping terms related by symmetry results in a favorable cancellation of Pauli terms and in an overall shorter circuit depth when time-evolving a state under their action.\n"
msgstr "Sa hakbang na ito, sinasamantala natin ang maraming symmetry na naroon sa electronic structure Hamiltonian sa pamamagitan ng pag-group ng mga magkakaugnay na term na may magkaparehong coefficient. Bagaman binabago nito ang operator coefficient distribution na pinagkukunan ng sample ng qDRIFT protocol, hindi nito naaapektuhan ang mga convergence guarantee nito. Higit sa lahat, ang pag-group ng mga term na magkakaugnay sa symmetry ay nagreresulta sa kanais-nais na pagkansela ng mga Pauli term at sa kabuuang mas maikling circuit depth kapag nag-time-evolve ng state sa ilalim ng pagkilos nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-fermions` provides the `group_terms_by_electronic_structure` function that does this grouping for us.\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang `qiskit-fermions` ng function na `group_terms_by_electronic_structure` na gumagawa ng grouping na ito para sa atin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the `group_terms_by_electronic_structure` assumes [normal ordering](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.html#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.normal_ordered) terms.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang `group_terms_by_electronic_structure` ay ipinapalagay na [normal ordering](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.html#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.normal_ordered) ang mga term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Filtering diagonal terms**\n"
msgstr "**Pag-filter ng mga diagonal term**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We remove the diagonal terms from the Hamiltonian used to generate the circuits, so that the $n$ qDRIFT sampling slots are spent on terms that move population between configurations. Such terms are best filtered out of the Hamiltonian at this point, before the `Evolution` gate is constructed in the next step.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis namin ang mga diagonal na term mula sa Hamiltonian na ginagamit sa pag-generate ng mga circuit, para ang $n$ qDRIFT sampling slot ay magamit sa mga term na naglilipat ng populasyon sa pagitan ng mga configuration. Pinakamainam na i-filter ang mga ganitong term mula sa Hamiltonian sa puntong ito, bago buuin ang `Evolution` gate sa susunod na hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms in question are the ones that are diagonal in the occupation-number basis, that is, the products of number operators $a^\\dagger_i a_i$. Three kinds of term fall under this description:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga term na tinutukoy ay ang mga diagonal sa occupation-number basis, ibig sabihin, ang mga produkto ng number operator na $a^\\dagger_i a_i$. Tatlong uri ng term ang pasok sa paglalarawang ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the **constant energy offset**, a product of zero number operators, whose time evolution contributes only a global phase;\n"
msgstr "ang **constant energy offset**, isang produkto ng zero na number operator, na ang time evolution ay nagbibigay lang ng global phase;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the **individual number operators** $n_i$, whose time evolution reduces to single-qubit $Z$ rotations;\n"
msgstr "ang mga **indibidwal na number operator** $n_i$, na ang time evolution ay nauuwi sa single-qubit na $Z$ rotation;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the **higher-order products** such as $n_i n_j$.\n"
msgstr "ang mga **higher-order na produkto** gaya ng $n_i n_j$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On their own, none of these move population between occupation-number configurations; they act only on the phases of the configurations already present. They are not inert, however: those relative phases feed into the interference generated by the excitation terms later in the circuit, so filtering them changes the evolution that is actually generated and can change the sampling distribution. This is a deliberate approximation in the circuit-generation step, made to focus sampling on excitation terms, rather than a step that leaves the sampled distribution untouched. Unlike the symmetry grouping above, which leaves the qDRIFT convergence guarantees intact, this filter changes the operator being evolved. The circuits therefore no longer approximate evolution under the full Hamiltonian, and the qDRIFT error bounds apply to the filtered operator rather than the original one. This is acceptable here because the circuits are only a sampling heuristic used to propose configurations: no term is lost from the energy estimate itself, since the filter applies only to the Hamiltonian used to build the circuits, while the classical diagonalization later uses the full Hamiltonian, diagonal terms included. SQD's accuracy depends on that classical step, which remains variational in the sampled subspace regardless of how the configurations were proposed.\n"
msgstr "Sa kanilang sarili, wala sa mga ito ang naglilipat ng populasyon sa pagitan ng mga occupation-number configuration; ang naaapektuhan lang nila ay ang mga phase ng mga configuration na naroon na. Gayunman, hindi sila walang epekto: ang mga relative phase na iyon ay nakakaapekto sa interference na nabubuo ng mga excitation term sa mas huling bahagi ng circuit, kaya ang pag-filter sa kanila ay nagbabago sa evolution na talagang nabubuo at maaaring magbago sa sampling distribution. Isa itong sinadyang approximation sa hakbang ng circuit generation, na ginawa para ituon ang sampling sa mga excitation term, at hindi isang hakbang na iniiwang buo ang sampled distribution. Hindi tulad ng symmetry grouping sa itaas, na nag-iiwang buo sa mga qDRIFT convergence guarantee, binabago ng filter na ito ang operator na ine-evolve. Kaya ang mga circuit ay hindi na nag-a-approximate ng evolution sa ilalim ng buong Hamiltonian, at ang mga qDRIFT error bound ay para sa na-filter na operator at hindi sa orihinal. Katanggap-tanggap ito dito dahil ang mga circuit ay isa lamang sampling heuristic na ginagamit para magmungkahi ng mga configuration: walang term na nawawala sa mismong energy estimate, dahil ang filter ay ina-apply lang sa Hamiltonian na ginamit sa pagbuo ng mga circuit, habang ang classical diagonalization sa bandang huli ay gumagamit ng buong Hamiltonian, kasama ang mga diagonal na term. Nakasalalay ang katumpakan ng SQD sa classical na hakbang na iyon, na nananatiling variational sa sampled subspace gaano man iminungkahi ang mga configuration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `filter_diagonal_terms()` function removes such terms from an operator in place. It identifies them from their normal-ordered structure — the multiset of creation modes matching the multiset of annihilation modes — so it is only valid on an operator that is already normal-ordered. This assumption is not checked at runtime.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis ng function na `filter_diagonal_terms()` ang mga ganitong term mula sa isang operator in place. Natutukoy nito ang mga ito mula sa kanilang normal-ordered na estruktura — ang multiset ng mga creation mode na tumutugma sa multiset ng mga annihilation mode — kaya valid lang ito sa operator na normal-ordered na. Hindi sinusuri sa runtime ang assumption na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have grouped the terms in the Hamiltonian, we will decide on the following parameters to generate the ensemble of circuits:\n"
"- The number of circuits to generate: `num_circuits`\n"
"- The length of each circuit in terms of excitation groups: `num_exc`\n"
"- The factor for the different evolution times: `times`\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayong napagsama-sama na natin ang mga term sa Hamiltonian, magpapasya tayo sa mga sumusunod na parameter para i-generate ang ensemble ng mga circuit:\n"
"- Ang bilang ng mga circuit na ige-generate: `num_circuits`\n"
"- Ang haba ng bawat circuit batay sa mga excitation group: `num_exc`\n"
"- Ang salik para sa iba't ibang evolution time: `times`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Creating fermionic circuits**\n"
msgstr "**Paglikha ng mga fermionic circuit**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now create fermionic circuits for each of the time-steps. Each circuit will consist of a single evolution gate, with the evolution time we declared earlier. The evolution operator is the Hamiltonian. Later we run transpiler passes on these circuits to create qDRIFT circuits.\n"
msgstr "Gagawa na tayo ngayon ng mga fermionic circuit para sa bawat time-step. Bawat circuit ay bubuuin ng iisang evolution gate, na may evolution time na idineklara natin kanina. Ang evolution operator ay ang Hamiltonian. Sa bandang huli, magpapatakbo tayo ng mga transpiler pass sa mga circuit na ito para gumawa ng mga qDRIFT circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ansatz preparation**\n"
msgstr "**Paghahanda ng ansatz**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the Hartree-Fock state using the `InitializeModes` class. For nitrogen, the process is simply applying X gates to the first `num_elec_a` qubits and then to the `num_elec_b` qubits, both of which equal to seven for nitrogen. This state represents the seven $\\alpha$ and seven $\\beta$ electrons of nitrogen.\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda natin ang Hartree-Fock state gamit ang class na `InitializeModes`. Para sa nitrogen, ang proseso ay simpleng pag-apply ng X gate sa unang `num_elec_a` na qubit at pagkatapos ay sa `num_elec_b` na qubit, na parehong pito para sa nitrogen. Kinakatawan ng state na ito ang pitong $\\alpha$ at pitong $\\beta$ na electron ng nitrogen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have our circuits, we will first use the passes available in `qiskit-fermions` to perform fermionic level optimizations, followed by transpiling our circuit for the backend of choice. Since this is a simulator experiment, we will first do this for the AerSimulator.\n"
"**Weight calculation for each group**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayong mayroon na tayong mga circuit, gagamitin muna natin ang mga pass na available sa `qiskit-fermions` para magsagawa ng mga optimization sa fermionic level, at pagkatapos ay i-transpile ang circuit natin para sa napiling backend. Dahil isa itong simulator experiment, gagawin muna natin ito para sa AerSimulator.\n"
"**Pagkalkula ng weight para sa bawat group**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this step, we perform the qDRIFT sampling of terms stochastically with probabilities proportional to their coefficients in the Hamiltonian. The qDRIFT transpiler pass does this for us. We can now create shallower circuits that can be executed on the hardware more efficiently despite limited qubit connectivity, even when the Hamiltonian contains long-range couplings and higher-than-quadratic terms.\n"
"After term grouping, it samples the operators based on their weights. For each operator $h_i$, the weight $W_{h_i}$ is defined as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa hakbang na ito, isinasagawa natin ang qDRIFT sampling ng mga term nang stochastic na may mga probability na proporsyonal sa kanilang mga coefficient sa Hamiltonian. Ito ay ginagawa para sa atin ng qDRIFT transpiler pass. Makakagawa na tayo ngayon ng mas mababaw na mga circuit na mas episyenteng maipapatakbo sa hardware sa kabila ng limitadong qubit connectivity, kahit na ang Hamiltonian ay may mga long-range coupling at mga term na higit sa quadratic.\n"
"Pagkatapos ng term grouping, sina-sample nito ang mga operator batay sa kanilang mga weight. Para sa bawat operator na $h_i$, ang weight na $W_{h_i}$ ay tinutukoy bilang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"W_{h_i} = |c_i| / \\lambda\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"W_{h_i} = |c_i| / \\lambda\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the terms were grouped in Step 1, each $h_i$ here is a whole group: $c_i$ is the mean absolute coefficient of the terms in group $i$, and each term in the group is evolved with its coefficient reduced to its sign.\n"
msgstr "Dahil napagsama-sama ang mga term sa Step 1, ang bawat $h_i$ dito ay isang buong group: ang $c_i$ ay ang mean absolute coefficient ng mga term sa group $i$, at ang bawat term sa group ay ine-evolve na ang coefficient ay binawasan hanggang sa sign nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fermionic and hardware-native optimizations**\n"
msgstr "**Mga fermionic at hardware-native na optimization**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function `generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()` returns a `MultiStagePassManager` that takes a `FermionicCircuit` and produces an optimized final circuit that we can transpile to run on our hardware. We replace its default optimization stage with a `FermionicPassManager` containing our `QDriftTrotterization` pass:\n"
msgstr "Ang function na `generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()` ay nagbabalik ng `MultiStagePassManager` na kumukuha ng `FermionicCircuit` at gumagawa ng na-optimize na final circuit na maaari nating i-transpile para tumakbo sa hardware natin. Pinapalitan natin ang default na optimization stage nito ng `FermionicPassManager` na naglalaman ng ating `QDriftTrotterization` pass:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `QDriftTrotterization` pass uses the weight-calculation and sampling internally to generate the circuits that we will use for sampling\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng `QDriftTrotterization` pass ang weight-calculation at sampling sa loob para i-generate ang mga circuit na gagamitin natin sa sampling\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `RelabelModes` pass is another optimization pass that can be used to permute the fermionic modes to optimize connectivity across qubits and reduce gate depth; read more in the [API reference](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes.html#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes)\n"
msgstr "Ang `RelabelModes` pass ay isa pang optimization pass na magagamit para i-permute ang mga fermionic mode para i-optimize ang connectivity sa mga qubit at bawasan ang gate depth; magbasa pa sa [API reference](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes.html#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The remaining stages of the `MultiStagePassManager` run automatically and handle the full fermion-to-qubit mapping:\n"
msgstr "Awtomatikong tumatakbo ang mga natitirang stage ng `MultiStagePassManager` at hinahawakan ang buong fermion-to-qubit mapping:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[F2QLayout](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout.html): The preset pass manager applies the `TrivialF2QLayout` pass, which trivially maps $n$ fermionic bits to $n$ qubits.\n"
msgstr "[F2QLayout](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout.html): Ina-apply ng preset pass manager ang `TrivialF2QLayout` pass, na trivial na nagma-map ng $n$ fermionic bit sa $n$ qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[F2QSynth](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.html): A transpilation pass to map fermion-based circuit instructions to qubit-based ones.\n"
msgstr "[F2QSynth](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-fermions/stable/0.1/stubs/qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.html): Isang transpilation pass para i-map ang mga fermion-based na circuit instruction sa mga qubit-based.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we are done with the fermionic-level optimizations, we can transpile the circuits for execution on the simulator.\n"
msgstr "Ngayong tapos na ang mga optimization sa fermionic level, maaari na nating i-transpile ang mga circuit para patakbuhin sa simulator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have our circuits, we can run them using Qiskit primitives on the AerSimulator. We will combine all the counts from different circuits. We convert them to boolean vectors before finally post-processing with SQD.\n"
msgstr "Ngayong mayroon na tayong mga circuit, maaari na nating patakbuhin ang mga ito gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive sa AerSimulator. Pagsasamahin natin ang lahat ng count mula sa iba't ibang circuit. Kino-convert natin ang mga ito sa mga boolean vector bago tuluyang i-post-process gamit ang SQD.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Using bitstrings for SQD**\n"
msgstr "**Paggamit ng mga bitstring para sa SQD**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run the diagonalization scheme on the selected bitstrings to find the lowest eigenvalue that will correspond to the ground state energy of the molecule. We create a callback function, declare initial occupancies, and set the parameters before finally running the diagonalization scheme. The callback function is used to print the current iteration and the current eigenvalue estimate at each iteration.\n"
msgstr "Maaari na nating patakbuhin ang diagonalization scheme sa mga napiling bitstring para hanapin ang pinakamababang eigenvalue na tutugma sa ground state energy ng molecule. Gumagawa tayo ng callback function, nagdedeklara ng mga initial occupancy, at itinatakda ang mga parameter bago tuluyang patakbuhin ang diagonalization scheme. Ginagamit ang callback function para i-print ang kasalukuyang iteration at ang kasalukuyang eigenvalue estimate sa bawat iteration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, to get the ground state estimate, we add the `nuclear_repulsion_energy` to the resultant energy.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, para makuha ang ground state estimate, idinadagdag natin ang `nuclear_repulsion_energy` sa nagresultang energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Note**: The subspace dimension is not fixed across iterations, even on the noiseless simulator — each subsample draws a different set of configurations, and the recovery step reshapes the pool between iterations, so the reported dimension varies from one subsample to the next. Noiseless sampling does not by itself pin the selected-subspace dimension. The hardware run, however, tends to give systematically larger subspaces, because noisy shots break particle-number symmetry and configuration recovery turns them into additional basis vectors. Because of that, we will also introduce another step for pruning bitstrings in the hardware section.\n"
msgstr "**Tandaan**: Hindi pirmi ang subspace dimension sa bawat iteration, kahit sa noiseless na simulator — bawat subsample ay gumuguhit ng ibang hanay ng mga configuration, at binabago ng recovery step ang pool sa pagitan ng mga iteration, kaya nag-iiba ang iniulat na dimension mula sa isang subsample hanggang sa susunod. Ang noiseless na sampling ay hindi nito mismong nagpapirmi sa dimension ng napiling subspace. Gayunman, ang hardware run ay may tendensiyang magbigay ng sistematikong mas malalaking subspace, dahil sinisira ng mga noisy shot ang particle-number symmetry at ginagawa ng configuration recovery na karagdagang basis vector ang mga ito. Dahil dito, magpapakilala rin tayo ng isa pang hakbang para sa pag-prune ng mga bitstring sa hardware section.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware example {#hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa hardware {#hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses 20 qubits (10 spatial orbitals). That choice is a convenience for a tutorial that should run quickly, not a hard ceiling on the method.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang halimbawang ito ng 20 qubit (10 spatial orbital). Pinili iyon para sa kaginhawahan ng isang tutorial na dapat tumakbo nang mabilis, hindi bilang mahigpit na hangganan ng pamamaraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost of the classical step is not set by the qubit count directly. SQD diagonalizes the Hamiltonian projected onto the subspace spanned by the *sampled* configurations, so what drives the classical cost is the dimension of that selected subspace — governed here by `samples_per_batch`, `num_batches`, and how many distinct configurations the circuits actually produce — together with the sparse linear algebra needed to apply the projected Hamiltonian. The full CI space grows combinatorially with orbitals and electrons, but the selected subspace is a small, tunable slice of it, and we control its size directly. Consequently, the number of qubits and the classical difficulty can be varied somewhat independently: a wider orbital space sampled into a modest subspace can be cheaper than a smaller system diagonalized over a very large one.\n"
msgstr "Ang gastos ng classical na hakbang ay hindi direktang itinatakda ng bilang ng qubit. Dina-diagonalize ng SQD ang Hamiltonian na naka-project sa subspace na sakop ng mga *na-sample* na configuration, kaya ang nagtatakda ng classical na gastos ay ang dimension ng napiling subspace — na dito ay pinamamahalaan ng `samples_per_batch`, `num_batches`, at kung ilang natatanging configuration ang talagang nagagawa ng mga circuit — kasama ang sparse linear algebra na kailangan para i-apply ang naka-project na Hamiltonian. Ang buong CI space ay lumalaki nang combinatorial kasabay ng mga orbital at electron, ngunit ang napiling subspace ay maliit at naaayos na bahagi nito, at direkta nating kinokontrol ang laki nito. Dahil dito, ang bilang ng qubit at ang classical na hirap ay maaaring baguhin nang medyo magkahiwalay: ang mas malawak na orbital space na sina-sample sa katamtamang subspace ay maaaring mas mura kaysa sa mas maliit na system na dina-diagonalize sa napakalaking subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, then, the feasible system size depends on the subspace dimension you need for the accuracy you want and on the memory and cores available to the eigensolver. Larger orbital spaces typically do require a larger subspace to reach chemical accuracy, and that is what eventually motivates distributed resources — see [qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc/) for scaling this step out. Rather than assuming a fixed cutoff, the practical approach is to watch the reported subspace dimension and the energy convergence across iterations and increase the subspace size until the energy stops improving or you exhaust available memory.\n"
msgstr "Sa praktika, ang magagawang laki ng system ay nakasalalay sa subspace dimension na kailangan mo para sa katumpakang gusto mo at sa memory at mga core na available sa eigensolver. Karaniwang nangangailangan ng mas malaking subspace ang mas malalaking orbital space para maabot ang chemical accuracy, at iyon ang sa huli ay nag-uudyok ng mga distributed resource — tingnan ang [qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc/) para i-scale out ang hakbang na ito. Sa halip na magpalagay ng nakapirming cutoff, ang praktikal na paraan ay bantayan ang iniulat na subspace dimension at ang energy convergence sa mga iteration at dagdagan ang laki ng subspace hanggang tumigil ang pagbuti ng energy o maubos ang available na memory.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note:* Due to sampling error from the noise in the hardware, the subspace created for diagonalization in the hardware run will be larger than what we get when using the simulator. While it increases the dimension of the subspace we want to diagonalize, the workflow still gives us an accurate answer due to the robustness of SQD towards noise.\n"
msgstr "*Tandaan:* Dahil sa sampling error mula sa noise sa hardware, ang subspace na nabuo para sa diagonalization sa hardware run ay magiging mas malaki kaysa sa makukuha natin gamit ang simulator. Bagama't pinalalaki nito ang dimension ng subspace na gusto nating i-diagonalize, nagbibigay pa rin ang workflow ng tumpak na sagot dahil sa tibay ng SQD laban sa noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pruning of spurious strings**\n"
msgstr "**Pag-prune ng mga spurious na string**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we can choose to perform an additional step. When we have all the bitstrings from the circuit executions, we can either filter out the invalid bitstrings before running SQD, or move forward without pruning. Skipping the pruning is generally preferable for hardware runs, because it leaves the symmetry-broken shots available to configuration recovery, which can repair them into valid configurations and thereby widen the subspace instead of discarding those shots outright.\n"
msgstr "Dito maaari tayong pumili na magsagawa ng karagdagang hakbang. Kapag mayroon na tayong lahat ng bitstring mula sa mga circuit execution, maaari nating i-filter ang mga di-valid na bitstring bago patakbuhin ang SQD, o magpatuloy nang walang pruning. Karaniwang mas mainam na laktawan ang pruning sa mga hardware run, dahil nananatiling magagamit ng configuration recovery ang mga shot na sira ang symmetry, na maaaring ayusin ang mga ito bilang mga valid na configuration at sa gayon ay palawakin ang subspace sa halip na tuluyang itapon ang mga shot na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since nitrogen can only have seven $\\alpha$ and seven $\\beta$ electrons, any bitstrings that have more or fewer than seven 1s in the first and the second half of the output can be discarded. We define a function that checks if the bitstrings are valid, and if not, discards them. Once we filter out the spurious bitstrings, the rest are sent into the diagonalization scheme. Use the `PRUNE` flag below to switch between the two behaviors.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang nitrogen ay maaari lang magkaroon ng pitong $\\alpha$ at pitong $\\beta$ na electron, anumang bitstring na may higit o kulang sa pitong 1 sa una at ikalawang kalahati ng output ay maaaring itapon. Nagde-define tayo ng function na sumusuri kung valid ang mga bitstring, at kung hindi, itinatapon ang mga ito. Kapag na-filter na natin ang mga spurious na bitstring, ang natitira ay ipinapadala sa diagonalization scheme. Gamitin ang `PRUNE` flag sa ibaba para magpalipat-lipat sa dalawang behavior.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind that pruning is only one of several choices that shape the final subspace, alongside the number of circuits, the set of evolution times, and diagonal-term filtering. Comparing a pruned run against an unpruned one is only informative if everything else is held fixed; the C++ version of [this tutorial](/tutorials/sqdrift) discusses this in more detail, since it postselects rather than recovers and also differs in those other parameters.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang pruning ay isa lang sa ilang pagpipiliang humuhubog sa pinal na subspace, kasama ng bilang ng mga circuit, ang hanay ng mga evolution time, at ang pag-filter ng diagonal term. Nagiging kapaki-pakinabang lang ang paghahambing ng pruned na run sa unpruned kung hindi nagbabago ang lahat ng iba pa; tinatalakay ito nang mas detalyado ng C++ na bersyon ng [tutorial na ito](/tutorials/sqdrift), dahil nagpo-postselect ito sa halip na nagre-recover at iba rin ang mga iba pang parameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you found this work interesting, you might be interested in the following material:\n"
"- [Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization) - a related tutorial using time-evolution circuits instead of a variational ansatz.\n"
"- [Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization) - a tutorial on how to construct a local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) circuit for quantum chemistry simulation.\n"
"- The [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) paper - the literature that this tutorial is based upon. (Note that some of the optimizations discussed in this paper are currently a work in progress, and this tutorial is subject to change in the future based on the evolution of the used libraries.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung naging kawili-wili sa iyo ang gawaing ito, maaaring interesado ka sa mga sumusunod na materyal:\n"
"- [Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization) - isang kaugnay na tutorial na gumagamit ng mga time-evolution circuit sa halip na variational ansatz.\n"
"- [Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization) - isang tutorial kung paano bumuo ng local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) circuit para sa quantum chemistry simulation.\n"
"- Ang paper na [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) - ang literaturang pinagbatayan ng tutorial na ito. (Tandaan na ang ilan sa mga optimization na tinalakay sa paper na ito ay kasalukuyang work in progress, at maaaring magbago ang tutorial na ito sa hinaharap batay sa pag-unlad ng mga ginamit na library.)\n"

